{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>A nurse from the Hebrew women.</b> Scripture teaches you that Moses refused to nurse from Egyptian women. And so the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: they took him and brought him to the Egyptian women, but he rejected their breasts. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: the mouth that is destined to speak with Me — shall it nurse from Egyptian women? As it is written (Isaiah 28:9): ״את מי יורה דעה ואת מי יבין שמועה גמולי מחלב עתיקי משדים״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:26.045891054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}